# data/ is 23 GB of CSV and Parquet. It lives in ADLS, not in the image.
# Without this line the build context alone would be larger than the credit.
data/

# Results and archives. Reproduced by running the pipeline, never shipped.
paper/archive/

# scripts/ is NOT excluded, and that is a change.
#
# It used to be, on the reasoning that scripts are development tooling. But the
# publication checker, the replay-bundle generator and the dataset verifier all
# have to run against CLOUD data, in this image, on a machine with no checkout.
# The first attempt to generate a replay bundle from the HI-Large scores failed
# with "can't open file /app/scripts/make_replay_bundle.py". An image that can
# run the pipeline but not the tooling that AUDITS the pipeline is half an
# image. They are a few tens of kilobytes of Python.

.venv/
.git/
.github/
infra/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Tests are deliberately NOT excluded: the image self-check is cheap, but being
# able to run the suite inside the built container is how we confirm the cloud
# environment behaves like the local one. That is Gate 4's whole purpose.

.DS_Store
*.log

# results_archive/ IS shipped now, and that is a reversal.
#
# "Reproduced by the pipeline, not needed in the image" was true of the
# pipeline and false of the AUDIT. The reproducibility tests recompute the
# published budget metrics from the replay bundles and check every derived
# artifact's provenance, and with the archive excluded they found nothing and
# skipped -- 31 skips in the image against 17 on the host, and the difference
# was the evidence. 13 MB.
#
# gold/ is the bulky part and carries the manifests the replay bundles are
# verified against, so it stays; only the retired duplicates below are cut.
results_archive/**/__pycache__/
